---
// OWNER APPROVAL: Jon approves this text before it is given to Google or anyone else as the publication's terms.
// Out of character, on purpose, like /privacy/: plain type, the real publisher, no seal. Every statement must stay true of
// the code: no accounts or purchases on the site; a commercial link carries a disclosure (src/modules/website/cta.ts).
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { author, site } from '../config/site';
import { breadcrumbJsonLd } from '../modules/website';
import { href } from '../lib/url';

const REVISED = 'November 2, 2026';
const h2 = 'mt-10 mb-3 text-featured font-bold';
const p = 'mt-3 max-w-prose';
const list = 'mt-3 grid list-disc gap-2.5 pl-[1.2em] [&>li]:max-w-prose';
---

<Base
  title={`Terms of use · ${site.name}`}
  description="The terms for reading this website and watching its videos: not professional advice, no warranty, and how to reuse the work."
  jsonLd={[breadcrumbJsonLd([{ name: 'Terms of use', path: '/terms/' }])]}
>
  <header class="grid gap-4 border-y-4 border-double py-5">
    <div class="eyebrow text-muted-foreground">
      <a class="text-muted-foreground no-underline hover:underline" href={href('/')}>{site.name}</a> · {
        site.publicRecord
      }
    </div>
    <h1 class="text-display font-bold">Terms of use</h1>
    <p class={`${p} text-muted-foreground`}>
      Last updated {REVISED}. {site.name} is an independent publication operated by {author.name}. By using this website
      or watching its videos, you accept these terms. If you do not accept them, please do not use it.
    </p>
  </header>

  <h2 class={h2} id="information">Information, not advice</h2>
  <ul class={list}>
    <li>
      Everything here is general information about public claims and published studies. It is not financial, legal,
      medical, engineering or other professional advice, and it does not consider your circumstances.
    </li>
    <li>
      The calculators give estimates from the figures you enter and the defaults they show. They are not quotes or
      predictions. Check anything important with a qualified professional before you act on it.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class={h2} id="accuracy">Accuracy</h2>
  <ul class={list}>
    <li>
      Findings are the publication's reading of the evidence it reviewed, prepared with the help of AI tools. They can
      be incomplete, out of date or wrong, and a confidence figure is not a guarantee.
    </li>
    <li>
      A finding is about a claim, not a judgment of the character or honesty of the person or organization who made it.
    </li>
    <li>
      The institutions, offices and seals on this site are inventions of the publisher. They are not government or
      regulatory bodies, and a finding is not an official ruling, certification or endorsement.
    </li>
    <li>
      To report an error, use <a href="#contact">the contact details below</a>. The
      <a href={href('/about/#publisher')}>About page</a> says how corrections are recorded.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class={h2} id="reuse">Reusing this work</h2>
  <p class={p}>
    You may read, share, link to and briefly quote this work if you credit {site.name}. Unless a licence in the
    <a href={site.repo}>public repository</a> says otherwise, all other rights are reserved. Quoted sources, cited studies
    and third-party data belong to their owners and stay under their own terms.
  </p>

  <h2 class={h2} id="other-sites">Other sites and services</h2>
  <p class={p}>
    Pages link to sources and services the publisher does not control and is not responsible for. Their own terms apply,
    including the <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms">YouTube Terms of Service</a> when you watch a video. A paid or
    commercial link is disclosed where it appears.
  </p>

  <h2 class={h2} id="liability">No warranty, and limits on liability</h2>
  <p class={p}>
    This website, its videos and its calculators are provided free of charge and "as is", without warranties of any
    kind. To the fullest extent the law allows, the publisher is not liable for any loss or damage arising from your use
    of them or your reliance on them. Nothing here limits a right or liability that the law does not allow to be
    limited.
  </p>

  <h2 class={h2} id="changes">Changes</h2>
  <p class={p}>
    The publisher may change or remove this content, or these terms, at any time. A change to these terms is recorded in
    the repository's history and applies from the date it is posted. The <a href={href('/privacy/')}>privacy policy</a> says
    how data is handled.
  </p>

  <h2 class={h2} id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p class={p}>
    Raise questions and corrections in the <a href={`${site.repo}/issues`}>repository's issues</a>. Issues are public,
    so leave personal details out; for anything private, send the publisher a message on
    <a href={author.links.LinkedIn}>LinkedIn</a> instead.
  </p>
</Base>
